{"id":"a5300dec-1b97-4448-be99-b514a5001ae6","object":"chat.completion","created":1784839077,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    # Validate nodes\\n    node_set = set(nodes)\\n    if len(node_set) != len(nodes):\\n        raise ValueError('duplicate node ids')\\n    \\n    # Validate core_distance\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f'missing core_distance for {n}')\\n    \\n    # Build mutual reachability edges\\n    edges_raw = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u not in node_set or v not in node_set:\\n            raise ValueError(f'node {u} or {v} not in nodes')\\n        if u == v:\\n            continue\\n        w = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        # Canonicalize undirected endpoints (lexicographic order)\\n        if u < v:\\n            edges_raw.append((u, v, w))\\n        else:\\n            edges_raw.append((v, u, w))\\n    \\n    # Sort: weight first, then source, then target\\n    edges_sorted = sorted(edges_raw, key=lambda x: (x[2], x[0], x[1]))\\n    \\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    selected_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    n_nodes = len(nodes)\\n    for u, v, w in edges_sorted:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            selected_edges.append({\\\"source\\\": u, \\\"target\\\": v, \\\"weight\\\": w})\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(selected_edges) == n_nodes - 1:\\n                break\\n    \\n    if len(selected_edges) != n_nodes - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('input graph is disconnected')\\n    \\n    return {\\\"edges\\\": selected_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": round(total_weight, 10)}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value as a Python source string for the function `solve(case)`. The function should compute mutual reachability MST via Kruskal with deterministic tie-breaking. Input: case dict with keys: nodes (list of node ids), core_distance (dict node->float), distances (list of [node1, node2, distance]). Output: dict with fields: edges (list of dicts with source, target, weight), total_weight (float).\n\nConstraints: Only standard library, no external calls, deterministic.\n\nSteps:\n1. Validate input: check nodes, core_distance, distances. Ensure all node ids in core_distance and distances refer to valid nodes.\n2. Build adjacency: for each pair in distances, compute mutual reachability = max(core_distance[src], core_distance[dst], dist). For undirected, canonicalize by sorting node ids (alphabetically?). The problem says \"canonicalize undirected endpoints\". Use tuple sorted lexicographically (since node ids are strings). Store (u, v, weight).\n3. Sort edges: primary key weight (float), secondary key u (string), tertiary key v (string). Use stable sort.\n4. Union-Find: with path compression and union by rank. Iterate sorted edges, if find(u) != find(v), union, add edge to result, accumulate total weight. Stop when selected edges = n-1.\n5. If after processing all edges, selected < n-1, raise ValueError(\"disconnected\").\n6. Return dict: edges list of dicts {\"source\": u, \"target\": v, \"weight\": weight}, \"total_weight\": total_weight.\n\nEdge cases: tie-breaking by weight, then node ids.\n\nImplementation details: Use classes or functions. Must not mutate input.\n\nWrite Python code as string, escape for JSON.\n\nNow produce the JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1656,"completion_tokens":1032,"total_tokens":2688,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":390},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":120},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}